# SDD Protocol — Air Finance App

This rule defines the Software Design Document (SDD) protocol that AI agents (Cursor, Claude Code) MUST follow when working in this repository.

## 1. Before writing any code

1. **Read the relevant documentation** listed in `CLAUDE.md` or `AGENTS.md` for the area you are modifying.
2. **Understand the existing pattern** by reading at least one neighboring file in the same directory.
3. **Check for existing implementations** — search before creating. Reuse > recreate.

## 2. File placement rules

| Artifact            | Location                                       | Naming                      |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Page component      | `apps/web/src/pages/<feature>/index.tsx`       | PascalCase export           |
| Page sub-components | `apps/web/src/pages/<feature>/components/`     | `<Feature><Part>.tsx`       |
| Page hooks          | `apps/web/src/pages/<feature>/hooks/`          | `use<Feature><Action>.ts`   |
| Global component    | `apps/web/src/components/` or `components/ui/` | PascalCase                  |
| Service             | `apps/web/src/services/<feature>Service.ts`    | camelCase                   |
| Hook (global)       | `apps/web/src/hooks/use<Name>.ts`              | camelCase with `use` prefix |
| Zustand store       | `apps/web/src/stores/<name>.ts`                | camelCase                   |
| Type                | `apps/web/src/types/<Name>.ts`                 | PascalCase                  |
| Utility             | `apps/web/src/utils/<name>.ts`                 | camelCase                   |
| Shared (cross-app)  | `packages/shared/src/`                         | Follow existing structure   |
| Route               | `apps/web/src/routes/`                         | Follow lazy import pattern  |

## 3. Component creation protocol

Every new page MUST follow this structure:

```
pages/<feature>/
├── index.tsx                    # Main page component
├── components/
│   ├── <Feature>Header.tsx
│   ├── <Feature>Filters.tsx
│   ├── <Feature>List.tsx
│   ├── <Feature>Card.tsx
│   ├── <Feature>EmptyState.tsx
│   └── <Feature>ErrorState.tsx
└── hooks/
    ├── use<Feature>Filters.ts
    └── use<Feature>Sorting.ts
```

Every page component MUST:

- Wrap content in `ViewDefault` (authenticated) or `LayoutAuth` (public)
- Handle loading, error, and empty states
- Be mobile-first responsive
- Support dark mode
- Use existing UI primitives from `components/ui/`

## 4. Data flow protocol

```
Route → Page → Custom Hook → Service (apiClient) → TanStack Query → UI
                                                  ↕
                                            Zustand Store (UI state only)
```

- Server state: TanStack Query (`useQuery`, `useMutation`)
- Client UI state: Zustand (sidebar, theme, active company, preferences)
- Form state: react-hook-form + zod schema
- NEVER mix server state in Zustand stores

## 5. TypeScript constraints

- `any` is FORBIDDEN — use explicit types or `unknown` with narrowing
- Use `??` instead of `||` for nullish coalescing
- Props interfaces MUST be `readonly`
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
- Export types from `types/` when shared across features

## 6. Styling constraints

- Mobile-first: base styles are for mobile; expand with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`
- Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid inline styles
- Use design system colors: `primary-*`, `text`, `card`, `border`, `background`
- Dark mode: always include `dark:` variants
- Touch targets: minimum 44x44px on mobile
- Use safe area utilities for fixed/absolute positioned elements

## 7. Quality gates

Before considering work complete:

1. `yarn typecheck` passes
2. `yarn lint` passes
3. Mobile viewport (375px) renders correctly
4. Dark mode works
5. Loading, error, and empty states are handled
6. No `any` types introduced
7. No unnecessary comments added
8. Existing patterns followed (not new abstractions without justification)

## 8. Harness — What to verify after changes

| Check           | Command / Method                            |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| TypeScript      | `yarn typecheck`                            |
| Linter          | `yarn lint`                                 |
| Build           | `yarn build`                                |
| Mobile layout   | Browser DevTools at 375px width             |
| Dark mode       | Toggle theme in app or browser              |
| Route works     | Navigate to the new/changed route           |
| API integration | Verify service calls match backend contract |

## 9. Forbidden actions

- Do NOT create files > 500 lines — refactor into modules
- Do NOT modify `.env` files without explicit user authorization
- Do NOT add new dependencies without checking if equivalent exists
- Do NOT use simulated/mock data outside of test files
- Do NOT skip ViewDefault layout for authenticated pages
- Do NOT use desktop-first responsive patterns
- Do NOT commit secrets or credentials
